            <div xml:id="d1192">

                <pb facs="1135" n="1123" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg1123"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">662.6731/169: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-31T13:00:00+02:00">March 31, 1943—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:53 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>606. In conversation yesterday with the Minister for Foreign Affairs he told me
                    that this [<hi rendition="#italic">at his?</hi>] first conference with Clodius
                    the latter had proposed a new agreement along the lines of the previous one.
                    Numan replied that he was not prepared to discuss a new agreement unless and
                    until prices had first been agreed upon. He said that for the time being Clodius
                    had accepted this point of view. Numan then remarked that he anticipated “great
                    difficulty” in agreeing with Clodius on prices and had little doubt that the
                    negotiations would “drag along” particularly as Mr. and Mrs. Clodius appeared to
                    be enjoying their visit to Ankara.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
